<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch bonds close lower, market awaits tap sales.</title>
<headline>Dutch bonds close lower, market awaits tap sales.</headline>
<text>
<p>---------------------(Snapshot at 1530 GMT)---------------------</p>
<p>*CASH YIELDS (Dutch state loans)</p>
<p> June 1999 7.50 pct   107.13/23 (+0.01)   bid yield 3.53 (n.a.)</p>
<p> Feb  2002		114.16/26 (-0.10)		 4.81 (+0.03)</p>
<p> Feb  2007 5.75 pct    99.48/58 (-0.24)		 5.82 (+0.04)</p>
<p> Jan  2023		111.67/87 (-0.39)		 6.55 (+0.04)</p>
<p>*FUTURES</p>
<p> BUNDS (June)	  100.70 (-0.24)</p>
<p> TREASURIES (June)   U.S. market closed today</p>
<p>*DM/NLG		    1.1245 (PREV 1.1243)</p>
<p>--------------------------(SPREADS)----------------------------</p>
<p>*DSLs versus Bunds  (pvs close)    *DSL curve     (pvs close)</p>
<p> 5 yr	 flat	 +0.01	  10-2 yr  229     (229)</p>
<p> 10 yr	-0.12	-0.08	  10-5 yr  101     (100)</p>
<p> Long	 -0.17	-0.16</p>
<p>-------------------------(May 26)-----------------------------</p>
<p>* Dutch bonds close lower as market lacks impetus with London and the U.S. closed by bank holiday.</p>
<p>* Market players await tomorrow's reopening of tap sales of ten-year bond. Already some business in grey market.</p>
